9294	{"artifactId":"HLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e","entry":{"id":"migrated-HLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:49:03.425Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"GitHub-only implementation and removal of compatibility support follow the revised upstream scope.","evidence":"The decision log's 'Scope rulings after the HLD review' explicitly narrows ac18 to GitHub and drops aliases, old body-marker readers, and the older-client half of ac29. These rulings support the HLD despite the broader original DEF wording. [files: docs/plans/core-data-model.md, .insrc/artifacts/DEF-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json]","action":"Keep the revised rulings linked from downstream designs.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing artifact heads are replaced atomically.","evidence":"writeArtifact calls writeAtomic; writeAtomic writes `${absPath}.tmp` with writeFileSync and then calls renameSync(tmp, absPath). This supports atomic replacement, though it does not establish a transaction spanning head and sidecar. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"Reuse the replacement primitive while separately specifying sidecar transaction recovery.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The delivery loader currently reads each recognized artifact file once.","evidence":"loadArtifactRecordSet enumerates files, performs one fs.readFile per recognized JSON file, parses it, and passes it to liftStoreFile. TESTS files are explicitly skipped. [files: src/workflow/delivery/load.ts]","action":"Preserve the single-pass property and explicitly add TESTS and the new artifact kinds to conversion verification.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"listComments and attach are new tracker-port operations, and GitHub is the existing adapter to extend.","evidence":"TrackerPort and IssueOps have neither operation. IssueOps exposes comment, readBody and writeBody instead. loadTracker constructs createGithubTracker, and the GitHub adapter implements issue operations through the gh wrappers. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Extend the existing port and GitHub factory, including their test doubles.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Keeping the existing writer-inventory test is sufficient to detect every new artifact writer.","evidence":"The detector's WRITER_NAMES is exactly ['writeArtifact', 'writeRecordFile', 'writeAtomic', 'writeFileSync', 'renameSync']. It does not recognize appendFileSync, appendRecord, or the proposed store.write. Merely keeping the test would allow new sidecar write paths to bypass its inventory checks. [files: src/workflow/artifact-write-inventory.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-write-inventory.test.ts]","action":"Assign an owner to extend the detector and negative controls for the new writer APIs and append primitives.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed RequirementIds.parse contract can preserve existing FR IDs while returning their epicHash.","evidence":"mintFrId stores only `E${utcDate(createdAtISO)}${hash8Of(epicHash)}`; hash8Of truncates to eight characters. parseFrId returns { date, hash8, story?, fr }, not a full epicHash. A pure parse(id) cannot recover the missing eight hash characters required by the proposed contract. [files: src/workflow/id.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/functional-definition.ts, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts]","action":"Preserve date and hash8 in the parsed FR type, or introduce an explicit repository-backed resolver with ambiguity handling. Keep existing FR strings valid.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed feedback shape can preserve existing inline anchors during conversion.","evidence":"Existing FeedbackAnchor includes quote, sectionSlug, prefix and suffix. The settled Gap 5 also includes prefix and suffix, but sc3 omits both. Conversion into that contract loses the context used to relocate a quote after edits. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/provenance/types.ts, docs/plans/core-data-model.md]","action":"Retain prefix and suffix in sc3 and specify the sectionSlug-to-section conversion.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Representing signoff state here while leaving team signoff behavior to the later team stories respects the upstream boundary.","evidence":"The DEF excludes changing team signoff, revision handling and tracker status sync. Gap 12 says 'Signoff (s7 to s9) waits for the new model'; the team inventory confirms those stories are not started. The current adapter still returns unsupported for reading signoff state. The HLD supplies structures without designing the external signoff workflow. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json, docs/plans/core-data-model.md, docs/plans/team-signoff-issues-inventory.md, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Keep external signoff creation, enforcement and tracker-status synchronization outside these stories.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"A log-ahead-of-head gap can always be completed by the next write using the specified records.","evidence":"sc3 records a revision number and content hash but no required content snapshot or replayable patch. Existing writeAtomic stores only the replacement bytes in a temporary file; it provides no durable recovery journal. If the process dies after appending the log and before writing the new head, the promised replacement content need not exist anywhere. A later unrelated write cannot reconstruct it from a hash. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, docs/plans/core-data-model.md, .insrc/artifacts/HLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json]","action":"Persist recoverable pending head content before committing the log, or require replay of the identical operation and refuse unrelated writes until recovery. Define crash handling at every write boundary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The specified feedback and tracker contracts support durable, once-only outbound posting.","evidence":"IssueOps.comment returns PortResult<void>; ghComment discards output. The HLD adds listComments and attach but no posting receipt or idempotency contract. Feedback is immutable and duplicate IDs are dropped, so appending the same feedback ID with a newly populated source does not define a durable update. A successful remote post followed by a crash before local recording can be posted again. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, docs/plans/core-data-model.md, .insrc/artifacts/HLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json]","action":"Define a durable append-only posting receipt keyed by feedback ID, a stable marker in outbound comments, and reconciliation through listComments before retrying an uncertain post.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The acceptance-to-test matrix covers all behavior required by ac7.","evidence":"The DEF's ac7 requires revision advancement, return to draft, and retention of the previous approval and review against the older revision. The HLD maps ac7 and ac8 only to 'revision moves only on a content hash change'. Existing writeArtifact handles numeric revision minting but does not implement those new lifecycle semantics, so revision-only assertions cannot verify ac7. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json, .insrc/artifacts/HLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json, src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"Expand the ac7 test mapping to assert draft status and preservation of prior decision records with their original revision bindings.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":4,"med":2,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-19T10:49:03.425Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
